<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11098" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coptŏs</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κοπτός, Κοπτώ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a trading town in the
				Thebaid, on the eastern side of the Nile</i>, afterwards <i>Justinianopolis</i>, now <i>Coft</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 9, 11, § 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 15,
			28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 16, 2</span></i>; Itin. Ant.
			p. 165, 6 al.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coptis</span></b> ,
			tĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κοπτίς</span>, <i>of
				Coptos</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 6, 9, §
			52</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coptītēs</span></b> ,
				ae, <i>adj. m.</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κοπτίτης</span>, <i>of
			Coptos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomos,</span>”
				<i>that of which Coptos was the capital</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 49</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coptītĭcus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of Coptos</i>, i. e. <i>Egyptian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adyta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 127, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
